# CASP15 H1171 — The Repair Crew Assembles (7PBL)
---

We've seen RuvB, the hexameric motor.

Now meet the full repair crew — RuvB bound
to a domain of RuvA, its partner protein
that recognizes damaged DNA.

Published in Nature in 2022.

> close
> load 7pbl
---

RuvA is the targeting system. It recognizes
Holliday junctions — the four-way DNA
crossover structures that form during
genetic recombination.

RuvA binds the junction and then recruits
RuvB to do the mechanical work.

> spin 0.15
---

The ATP molecules are still here, powering
the complex.

But now we can see how RuvA's domain
docks onto the RuvB ring, creating a
functional machine that can both find
and fix damaged DNA.

> stop
> view ligand
---

This assembly represents a prediction challenge
beyond simple docking — it's protein-protein
interaction combined with ligand binding.

CASP15 tested whether methods could predict
not just where the ligand goes, but how
the whole complex comes together.

> reset
> spin 0.1
---

The RuvB-RuvA complex — DNA repair in action.
PDB code 7PBL, CASP15 target H1171.

> stop
